        prov:wasAssociatedWith <http://example.org/node/orchestrator> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing. The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3. Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, to achieve a response time of less than 2 seconds, our need to ensure our architecture is optimized for low latency. our typical RAG p95 response time is 1800 ms, which is close to the requirement, but our may need to fine-tune our models or optimize our architecture to meet the requirement. For 99.9% availability, our have achieved 99.92% availability in past projects, so our are close to meeting 99.9% availability. our can propose an architecture that uses redundant components and auto-scaling to ensure high availability. To meet the hosting requirements, our can use our experience with SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure providers such as Outscale, which is within the EU and has no dependency on non-European suppliers. our propose an architecture that uses a combination of our existing technologies, including LangChain or LlamaIndex for RAG, Qdrant or Weaviate for vector databases, and vLLM or Ollama for inference servers. our can use Terraform or Ansible for infrastructure-as-code deployment on Outscale, which is within the EU and has no dependency on non-European suppliers SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For API integration, our can use our experience with API gateways like Kong or Apigee to integrate with civil-status and town-planning software, EDM systems, and user directories. our will need to conduct a thorough audit of the legacy APIs to ensure seamless integration. Overall, while our current stack can partially meet the client's requirements, our will need to optimize and fine-tune our architecture to achieve the required response time and availability." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The total contract value is 3 million euros over 4 years, with an annual cost of exploitation that must remain controlled and compatible with the municipal budget capacity. The client expects cost optimization without sacrificing quality. Are we financially eligible to bid, and what is the projected margin?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What approach can we propose to optimize costs while guaranteeing the expected quality of service? we are financially eligible to bid as we max contract value eligibility is 3 million euros, which matches The total contract value, and we have met the minimum turnover threshold. To determine the projected margin, we need to consider the pricing model, specifically the target gross margin percentage, which is 28%. However, without knowing the exact costs associated with this project, we cannot calculate the projected margin." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "But we can propose an approach to optimize costs while maintaining quality. we can absorb a certain level of budget reduction through rate renegotiation with subcontractors, as indicated by we cost sensitivity data. we can also consider scope reduction if necessary, such as removing optional modules or reducing training days, to maintain profitability while still delivering the required quality of service. Given The client expectation for cost optimization without sacrificing quality, we could propose a flexible pricing model that takes into account the municipal budget capacity and we own cost structure, potentially incorporating elements like milestone-based payments and performance-based incentives to ensure both parties' interests are aligned." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk15> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires strict GDPR compliance (EU-only hosting, no data transfer outside EU, encryption of sensitive data). All AI recommendations must be explainable post-hoc. No automated decision is allowed without explicit agent validation. What legal risks should we flag, and are we compliant?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk16> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Can we current contractual framework accommodate the client's requirements? Based on the provided context, we appears to have a good foundation for GDPR compliance, given we experience with EU institutions and jurisdictions, as well as we awareness of AI regulatory knowledge, including transparency obligations and human oversight. The fact that all operations are intra-EU and no Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) or adequacy decisions are required is also positive. However, we should flag the following legal risks:  - Ensuring continuous compliance with evolving GDPR requirements,  - Maintaining the explainability of AI recommendations,  - Strict adherence to the no automated decision-making without human validation policy. our current contractual framework seems to accommodate some of the client's requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk17> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For instance, we standard IP model and source code escrow capability can help mitigate vendor lock-in risks. Additionally, we awareness of prohibited AI practices and commitment to human oversight and validation align with the client's AI-related requirements. To fully comply with the tender requirements, we should ensure that we data processing practices strictly adhere to GDPR principles, focusing on EU-only hosting and encryption of sensitive data. Since we standard legal basis for GDPR compliance is Article 6(1)(e), performance of a task in the public interest, this may need review depending on the specific nature of the contract." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk18> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, while there are areas where our current contractual framework aligns with the client's requirements, careful review and potential adjustments to we contractual and operational practices are necessary to ensure full compliance with the specified conditions." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk19> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must guarantee a strict compliance with GDPR, ensure data protection (hosting exclusively on EU territory, no data transfer outside EU, encryption of sensitive data), and provide explicability and transparency for AI recommendations. How can we ensure these security and regulatory requirements are met, and what measures do we need to implement? To guarantee strict compliance with GDPR and meet the specified security and regulatory requirements, several measures must be implemented. Firstly, hosting data exclusively on EU territory is already ensured as our standard data residency is EU only. Additionally, cross-border transfer of data is prohibited by default unless an explicit legal basis exists, which aligns with the requirement of no data transfer outside EU." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk2> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained. It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents. To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk20> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For data protection, sensitive data must be encrypted. While the context does not explicitly mention encryption of sensitive data at rest or in transit, the context highlights the use of anonymisation tools such as Microsoft Presidio and custom NER models for data anonymization, which is a step towards protecting personal data. To provide explicability and transparency for AI recommendations, measures such as output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, and confidence threshold escalation are already in place. The model isolation approach, where inference API access is provided without direct model access to end users, further enhances security. Moreover, the implementation of a Data Protection Impact Assessment (DPIA) capability with an average duration of 3 weeks for such assessments ensures that data protection considerations are thoroughly evaluated for new projects or significant changes." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk21> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The appointment of a GDPR Data Protection Officer (DPO), reachable at dpo@nexus-engineering.it, also underscores the commitment to GDPR compliance. Lastly, ensuring explicability in AI recommendations could involve maintaining detailed logs of AI decision-making processes and providing clear, understandable explanations of how these decisions are reached, though specific measures for achieving this are not detailed in the provided context. Regular security audits, including annual penetration testing and post-major release testing, help identify vulnerabilities early on. In summary, while several necessary measures are already in place or planned, such as data residency within EU, anonymization tools, AI security controls, and GDPR compliance mechanisms, ensuring encryption of sensitive data and enhancing explicability and transparency for AI recommendations are key areas to focus on. Implementing these requirements will help ensure that the solution meets all specified security and regulatory demands." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk22> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client expects a solution that provides intelligent assistance to municipal agents, including search for information, help with drafting letters or answers, accompaniment in file instruction, and suggestion of actions. Can our current AI capabilities meet these requirements, and what innovation strategy can our propose to enhance the solution? our current AI capabilities can partially meet The client requirements. our have experience with large language models, including Mistral 7B, which can be fine-tuned for tasks such as search, drafting letters, and suggesting actions. our Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities can also help with retrieving relevant information to assist municipal agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk23> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, to fully meet The client expectations, our would need to enhance the solution. our innovation pipeline is currently exploring topics such as knowledge graphs for procedural reasoning and multi-agent collaboration frameworks, which could be leveraged to improve the intelligent assistance provided to municipal agents. our can propose an innovation strategy that builds upon Our Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities and explores the application of knowledge graphs to model municipal procedures and regulations. This would enable the AI system to provide more accurate and context-specific suggestions and accompaniment to municipal agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk24> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, our could investigate the use of multi-agent collaboration frameworks to facilitate seamless interactions between human agents and the AI system. By leveraging our current AI capabilities and investing in research and development, our can propose a solution that meets The client requirements and provides a competitive advantage in the market. our typical timeline for developing and refining such a solution would be around 9 months, from version 1 to version 2, which is in line with Our innovation pipeline TRL levels 6, 7, and 8." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk25> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client wishes to limit the environmental footprint of The client information systems, with a focus on reducing energy consumption and relying on low-carbon-impact infrastructures. How can our proposed solution contribute to limit, and what eco-friendly practices can our implement? our, can contribute to limit by proposing solutions that utilize green hosting partners, such as OVHcloud or Scaleway, both of which use 100% renewable energy. our can also implement digital sobriety practices like INT8/INT4 model quantisation to reduce GPU energy consumption by approximately 40%, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, and query result caching to reduce recomputes by around 20%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk26> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, our green IT hardware procurement policy ensures a minimum 5-year lifecycle for equipment. By leveraging these capabilities, our can help reduce the client's environmental footprint and lower the client's energy consumption." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk27> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Typically, our solutions achieve an energy reduction of about 35% compared to baseline scenarios." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk28> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "**Executive Summary** Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with specialized agents, proposes a comprehensive solution to implement an artificial intelligence (AI) assistance tool for the City of Belval's municipal agents. proposes integrates technical architecture, security and regulatory compliance, legal framework, budget optimization, AI innovation, and CSR sustainability to meet the client's requirements. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. leverage Nexus Engineering S.r.l. experience with API integration, EDM systems, user directories, SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure, and large language models to provide an intelligent assistance tool that facilitates access to information, improves answer quality, and reduces processing times. **Understanding of Requirements** Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have carefully reviewed the City of Belval's call for tenders and understand the need for an AI solution that assists municipal agents in municipal agents daily missions. a comprehensive solution to implement an artificial intelligence (AI) assistance tool for the City of Belval's municipal agents must cover functionalities such as assistance with consultation of information, drafting, instruction of files, and collaboration and continuity of processing. Additionally, a comprehensive solution to implement an artificial intelligence (AI) assistance tool for the City of Belval's municipal agents must comply with regulatory requirements, including GDPR, and ensure data protection, explicability, and transparency. **Proposed Solution** a comprehensive solution to implement an artificial intelligence (AI) assistance tool for the City of Belval's municipal agents integrates the following components: * Technical Architecture: Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will use a combination of LangChain or LlamaIndex for RAG, Qdrant or Weaviate for vector databases, and vLLM or Ollama for inference servers. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. architecture will be optimized for low latency, with a target response time of less than 2 seconds, and high availability, with an objective of 99.9% uptime. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will use Terraform or Ansible for infrastructure-as-code deployment on Outscale's SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure. * Security and Regulatory Compliance: Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will ensure strict compliance with GDPR requirements, including hosting data exclusively on EU territory, prohibiting cross-border transfer of data, and encrypting sensitive data." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk29> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will also provide explicability and transparency for AI recommendations through measures such as output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, and confidence threshold escalation. * Legal Framework: Nexus Engineering S.r.l. contractual framework will accommodate the client's requirements, including Nexus Engineering S.r.l. standard IP model and source code escrow capability to mitigate vendor lock-in risks. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will ensure that Nexus Engineering S.r.l. data processing practices strictly adhere to GDPR principles and focus on EU-only hosting and encryption of sensitive data. * Budget Optimization: Nexus Engineering S.r.l. propose a flexible pricing model that takes into account the municipal budget capacity and Nexus Engineering S.r.l. own cost structure, potentially incorporating elements like milestone-based payments and performance-based incentives. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. target gross margin percentage is 28%, and Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can absorb a certain level of budget reduction through rate renegotiation with subcontractors. * AI Innovation: Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will leverage Nexus Engineering S.r.l. existing RAG capabilities and explore the application of knowledge graphs to model municipal procedures and regulations. This will enable the AI system to provide more accurate and context-specific suggestions and accompaniment to municipal agents. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. innovation pipeline is currently exploring topics such as multi-agent collaboration frameworks, which could be leveraged to improve the intelligent assistance provided. * CSR Sustainability: Nexus Engineering S.r.l. propose solutions that utilize green hosting partners, such as OVHcloud or Scaleway, both of which use 100% renewable energy." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk3> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7. Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8. Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk30> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will implement digital sobriety practices like INT8/INT4 model quantisation to reduce GPU energy consumption by approximately 40%, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, and query result caching to reduce recomputes by around 20%. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. green IT hardware procurement policy ensures a minimum 5-year lifecycle for equipment. **Unaddressed Requirements** None of the requirements specified in the call for tenders are left unaddressed. However, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. note that some aspects, such as the exact costs associated with the project and the detailed measures for achieving explicability and transparency in AI recommendations, will require further discussion and clarification with the client. **Conclusion** Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with specialized agents, is confident that Nexus Engineering S.r.l. proposed solution meets the City of Belval's requirements for an AI assistance tool. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. believe that Nexus Engineering S.r.l. integrated approach, leveraging technical architecture, security and regulatory compliance, legal framework, budget optimization, AI innovation, and CSR sustainability, will provide a comprehensive and effective solution for municipal agents. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. look forward to discussing our proposed solution in further detail with the client and exploring how Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can work together to achieve the project objectives." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk4> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk5> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing. The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3. Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk6> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained. It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents. To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk7> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7. Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8. Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
